            <ArticleTitle>Solitary osteochondroma causing popliteal pseudoaneurysm that presented as a mass lesion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteochondromas are the most frequently occurring bone tumors and can rarely lead to vascular complications. A 14-year-old boy with solitary exostosis of the right femur presented with a mass lesion at the posterior aspect of the thigh. Radiological studies demonstrated a popliteal artery pseudoaneurysm. In this case report, radiological findings of this lesion are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
